YN8CVXB", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55658, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LK6Sd1Czku1tRYwYN8CVXB", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57818, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_017gyT4gT2SjYbDbUXmQscLu", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58118, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017gyT4gT2SjYbDbUXmQscLu", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58118, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017gyT4gT2SjYbDbUXmQscLu", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63189, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions and healthy again. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%. I also opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Version choice:** v2.3.1 is unhealthy and so is v2.3.1-rc, so v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a healthy version is safe to repeat, so I ran it again and it worked in all three regions. A status check afterwards confirmed the service is healthy.\n- **Incident:** The create request timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and saw it had gone through, so the on-call wasn't paged twice. It explains the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure) and the current state.\n\nTwo things still need follow-up, both noted in the incident: finding out why v2.3.1 failed, and looking into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JN7aM4KqFY7y8gvC2jJGWm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015y9vDWQjHdnWaKUArvtExL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01775g7oZXpphZTg6Fap2uUF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Tuz485x7UGEimX6NXS74Rf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway. Rolling back to a known-healthy version is safe to repeat, so I'll try once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013y6fGXk131i7qcixYg9jYX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BWnGAhvmVNiMs28LvobEHm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016DxAWB4NjsmXN7a1iBT2pq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LK6Sd1Czku1tRYwYN8CVXB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with error rate ~18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release marked healthy (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy, so it was skipped). The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A second rollback succeeded. All regions are now on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the incident may or may not have been created. I'll check before retrying so the on-call doesn't get paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017gyT4gT2SjYbDbUXmQscLu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions and healthy again. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%. I also opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Version choice:** v2.3.1 is unhealthy and so is v2.3.1-rc, so v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a healthy version is safe to repeat, so I ran it again and it worked in all three regions. A status check afterwards confirmed the service is healthy.\n- **Incident:** The create request timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and saw it had gone through, so the on-call wasn't paged twice. It explains the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure) and the current state.\n\nTwo things still need follow-up, both noted in the incident: finding out why v2.3.1 failed, and looking into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}